6. Adequate organ function defined as:1) Creatinine clearance (as estimated by Cockcroft Gault) \>60 mL/min. 2) Serum ALT/AST\ 92% on room air. 7) pulmonary function: ventilation function is normal or is restricted mildly.
7. Females of reproductive age must be in non-lactation period. Females of childbearing potential must have a negative serum or urine pregnancy test. All subjects must use medical-approved-contraception (such as intrauterine device and contraceptive drugs) during the period of trial and in 6 months after cell transfusion therapy.
