Exclusion Criteria:

1. Pre-existing or clinically significant CNS disorders not due to lupus at the time of screening, such as convulsive seizures, epilepsy, epileptic seizures, cerebrovascular disease (ischemia/hemorrhage), cerebral edema, reversible posterior leukoencephalopathy, paralysis, aphasia, stroke, severe brain injury, dementia, Parkinson's disease, cerebellar disorders, organic brain syndromes, encephalitis, CNS vasculitis, or psychiatric disorders; epilepsy due to lupus, stable without seizures for a period of 1 year prior to the screening period Stable seizure-free for 1 year may also be screened.
